10	// That matters more than a `.mem` file does. A real wiki holds tiddlers, not files on disk, and a
11	// tiddler's `type` field is the only place it can announce its dialect. `firstLine` cannot reach
12	// this — it reads line one, where `title:` stands — so the declaration has to be read where it
13	// actually sits, by the grammar, in the header.
